  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "service",
      "title": "Request processing",
      "items": [
        "Reference-application quotas wrap the route mux and run before certificate extraction and body decoding. Configured route families use atomic per-peer and aggregate buckets in shared protocol state.",
        "Quota exhaustion returns 429 with Retry-After; unavailable quota state returns 503. The reusable service does not install this middleware."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "failure",
      "title": "Certificate status before service hooks",
      "items": [
        "Both check-in and command connections check the configured certificate-status callback inside Core before hooks, replacement handling or ordinary dispatch. A rejection publishes CertificateStatusRejected and maps to HTTP 403.",
        "The reference composition enables revocation enforcement by default. Transport certificate extraction, status checks, pinning and enrollment/account authorization remain separate responsibilities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "service",
      "title": "Extension points",
      "items": [
        "DMHandler connects the service to declarative management without importing the engine. UserVerifier supplies user-channel authentication policy.",
        "After the status gate and hooks, a pending replacement handles permitted candidate traffic before ordinary dispatch; unrelated traffic still needs the appropriate identity authorization.",
        "SQL outcome capture commits with participating local mutations. Native webhooks also observe public protocol requests and replies; exchange capture runs after the handler. Slog and in-process subscribers remain ephemeral.",
        "Sensitive JSON/raw export requires root-managed subscriptions and encrypted retention. Revision changes pause old backlog; replay uses retained representations. The protocol library has no webhook transport dependency."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "transport",
      "title": "Public documentation",
      "items": [
        "Check-in \u2014 https://developer.apple.com/documentation/devicemanagement/check-in",
        "Sending MDM commands to a device \u2014 https://developer.apple.com/documentation/devicemanagement/sending-mdm-commands-to-a-device",
        "Declarative Management check-in \u2014 https://developer.apple.com/documentation/devicemanagement/declarative-management",
        "Native webhook contract and JSON examples \u2014 https://github.com/deploymenttheory/go-apple-dm/blob/main/docs/operations/webhooks.md"
      ]
    }
  ]
